    "read": "Equity fell $100.0m in 2025 while the company earned $228.2m, so capital returned exceeded net income. That is not repeatable indefinitely. Equity to assets is 7.4% and assets grew 7.2% in 2025 to within $647.6m of the cap. If assets keep drifting toward $10bn the bank must hold more capital, not less, and the payout ratio has to fall below 100%. The buyback is bounded by regulatory capital, not by earnings, and the base case reflects that with a 95% payout rather than the 100%+ of 2025."
