    "read": "Management's own guidance implies net income must grow by roughly 30% between 2026 and 2027, because the repurchase can only supply about 4.6 points of the 36.7% earnings-per-share step. Net income has grown 13.1%, 4.9% and an estimated 8.7% in the three prior years. The 2027 target is therefore not an extrapolation of the established business plus buyback; it requires a step change in fintech revenue that has not yet appeared in reported results."
